cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AtlasGB — evidenced memory maps for Game Boy cartridges"
message: >-
  If you use an atlas from this project, a citation is appreciated but not
  required. What is most useful to the next person is a link, so they can check
  the evidence for themselves. Please name the atlas you used — an address is a
  fact about one cartridge, and a citation that does not say which one is not
  much of a citation.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "The AtlasGB contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alchemy86/AtlasGB"
url: "https://github.com/Alchemy86/AtlasGB"
abstract: >-
  A project publishing machine-readable memory maps of Game Boy cartridges,
  one atlas per cartridge under atlases/, in which every entry carries the
  evidence that supports it. One atlas is published: Pokémon Red and Blue
  (English, USA/Europe) — 2,898 evidenced claims covering video RAM, cartridge
  RAM, work RAM, high RAM and the cartridge's own data tables, with work RAM
  and high RAM 100% accounted for and no holes. Unlike every other published
  Generation 1 memory map, each entry names how it was checked — found as an
  instruction operand in the cartridge image, observed to change on a running
  cartridge under a fixed script, or proved by a named invariant — and the
  seven entries with no evidence say so rather than borrowing confidence from
  the rows beside them.
keywords:
  - "Game Boy"
  - "memory map"
  - "reverse engineering"
  - "emulation"
  - "Pokémon"
  - "dataset"
license: MIT
references:
  - type: data
    title: "AtlasGB — Pokémon Red and Blue"
    abstract: >-
      Every address in Pokémon Red and Blue (English, USA/Europe), with the
      evidence for it. 2,898 claims; 2,842 of them in storage regions, of which
      1,594 are named by the cartridge, 2,694 were observed live, 36 are covered
      by an invariant, and 7 carry no evidence and say so.
    authors:
      - name: "The AtlasGB contributors"
    url: "https://github.com/Alchemy86/AtlasGB/tree/main/atlases/pokemon-rb"
    license: MIT
